      "reason": "#892: `supported_locales` went from four to ten, so the ledger asks whether any observation record covers each surface in these six languages. None does, and no derivation can change that: a surface census is a READING taken on a running Logic, and this repository has run Korean, Japanese, German and English. That is the honest difference between this axis and the coverage one -- a label's ten languages come from Apple's rows, and a census of what the mixer looks like on a Spanish Logic does not. These were always absent; the ledger simply had no column to say so. They may only shrink from here, and each closes when somebody runs that language and files a census."
    },
    "undocumented_variants": {
      "date": "2026-09-18",
      "members": [
        "cycleRangeEnd→끝"
      ],
      "reason": "#892: `끝` is the Korean literal the cycle-locator matcher has shipped with, and moving it out of `AccessibilityChannel+Transport.swift` and into a LabelSet is what made the ledger able to see it. It is undocumented in the exact sense the ledger means: no row in Apple's ten-locale corpus carries `끝` -- Apple's `End` is `종료` -- and a full AX walk of the 1334 elements a running Logic 12.3 ko-KR exposes on 2026-09-18 found exactly two naming the cycle, the control-bar AXCheckBox `사이클` and the ruler's AXLayoutItem `사이클 리전`, neither a text field. So the field this literal was written for has never been observed and the literal is a value of nothing. It is KEPT rather than replaced by `종료` because replacing an unproved reading with a proved non-reading would narrow a Korean match on no evidence; the four English direction words beside it (`in`, `left`, `out`, `right`) were dropped instead, since the list of literals answered nowhere in Logic may only shrink and three of the four had just joined it."
    },
    "unmeasured_coverage.es-ES": {
      "date": "2026-09-25",
      "members": [
        "pluginMenuAudioUnits",
        "stemExportProgressWindowTitle"
